  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Abram heard that his brother was taken captive, Gen. 14:14. Tiglath-pileser … carried them captive, 2 Kgs. 15:29. the king of Babylon brought captive to Babylon, 2 Kgs. 24:16. which ye have taken captive of your brethren, 2 Chr. 28:11. thou hast led captivity captive, Ps. 68:18 (Eph. 4:8). they shall take them captives, whose captives they were, Isa. 14:2 (2 Ne. 24:2). Even the captives of the mighty shall be taken, Isa. 49:25. captive exile hasteneth that he may be loosed, Isa. 51:14. he hath sent me … to proclaim liberty to the captives, Isa. 61:1 (Luke 4:18; D&C 138:18, 31, 42). Judah shall be carried away captive, Jer. 13:19. Judah … carry them captive into Babylon, Jer. 20:4. Nebuzar-adan … carried away captive of the Jews, Jer. 52:30. I was among the captives, Ezek. 1:1.",
